# Slice 334 (the author 2026-11-09: `name := "test"` names the part explicitly whatever callable name exists): with the
# function name declared, `fn: name := k3; ...` still binds the part name by its name and creates k3; name stays the
# callable it is (name(2) 200, one call).
fn: name (int: x) int (int: calls 0)
    calls := calls + 1
    return: x * 100
end: name
fn: name := k3; args := (int: a); return := int; body := (return: a + 2)
int: r1 k3(1)
int: r2 name(2)
int: c name\var\calls
